# Running the Tests

The suite relies on `pytest` and `json5`. Some tests also require the optional
[`dspy`](https://pypi.org/project/dspy-ai/) package. Those tests will be skipped
if `dspy` isn't installed.

Install dependencies and run the tests with:

```bash
pip install -e .
pip install -r requirements.txt
# optional: install dspy for the full suite
pip install dspy-ai
pytest
```

## Selecting Tests

Use the `-k` flag to run only tests matching a given expression. This lets you
focus on a single module or feature:

```bash
pytest -k "cli or registry"
```

Running a subset can dramatically reduce runtimes when resources are limited.

## Low Resource Tips

If `pytest-xdist` is installed the suite can run in parallel:

```bash
pytest -n auto
```

Limit the number of workers (e.g. `-n 1`) or combine it with `-k` to keep CPU
and memory usage under control.

The CI workflow installs the runtime requirements with
`pip install -r requirements.txt` before running the tests.
Running the same command locally ensures your environment matches the
automated checks.

## CLI Fixtures and Stubs

The Typer-based `tino` CLI tests use a shared `tino_cli_runner` fixture along
with `fake_http_service` to intercept outbound HTTP traffic. The latter
provides a `stub(method, path, payload)` helper so tests can emulate Task
Cascadence, docs publishing, or other services without reaching the network.
Telemetry assertions rely on patching `telemetry.record_event`; see
`tests/test_tino_cli_services.py` for examples.

Tauri command handler tests install a temporary Python module via the
`TINO_BRIDGE_RECORD` environment variable to capture command arguments. The
Rust fixtures are self-contained, but you can replicate the behaviour by
running `cargo test --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml` locally.

## Tauri Tests

The CI pipeline also compiles the Tauri application in release mode to run a
basic window test. The test will be skipped if the required GTK libraries are
missing. Build and test it locally with:

```bash
cargo test --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml --release
```
